---
import { getYearsOfExperience } from "@/consts";

const programmingLangs = [
  { src: "languages/typescript.png", alt: "TypeScript" },
  { src: "languages/react.png", alt: "React" },
  { src: "languages/python.png", alt: "Python" },
  { src: "languages/nodejs.png", alt: "Node.js" },
];
---

<article
  class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 md:flex-row"
>
  <div
    class="[&>p]:mb-4 [&>p>strong]:text-emerald-500 dark:[&>p>strong]:text-emerald-100 [&>p>strong]:font-normal [&>p>strong]:font-mono text-pretty"
  >
    <p>
      My name is Carlos Jiménez, a <strong>Systems Engineer</strong> graduated from the Instituto
      Tecnológico de Santo Domingo (INTEC), with over <strong
        ><span id="years-exp-about">{getYearsOfExperience()}</span> years of professional experience</strong
      > building scalable and high-performance web applications across the full stack.
    </p>

    <p>
      I am deeply passionate about <strong>technology and innovation</strong>, and I thrive in
      collaborative environments where I can apply my expertise while continuously growing. I enjoy
      transforming complex problems into clean, efficient, and maintainable solutions.
    </p>

    <p>
      Throughout my career I have worked with a wide range of technologies — from responsive
      frontends with <strong>React and Next.js</strong> to robust backend services with
      <strong>Java Spring Boot, Python, and Node.js</strong>. I am always exploring new tools and
      frameworks to stay at the forefront of the industry.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-8 w-40 md:w-96 md:mb-10">
    {
      programmingLangs.map((lang) => (
        <img
          class="transition-all duration-300 hover:scale-110 hover:rotate-6 shadow-md"
          src={lang.src}
          alt={lang.alt}
        />
      ))
    }
  </div>
</article>

<script>
  import { getYearsOfExperience } from "@/consts";

  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", () => {
    const yearsSpan = document.getElementById("years-exp-about");
    if (yearsSpan) {
      yearsSpan.textContent = getYearsOfExperience().toString();
    }
  });
</script>
